From 3a439ccfea60c333986fed8308c23962a4b25b85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:10:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the reason for level 3 of the IPT tunnel,
 with the whole colour

The comment gave codes of I alone, a measure that leaves out P and T of the
right pixel of a pair. Measured over I, P and T of every pixel, the composer's
YCbCr that level 3 sends loses nothing against IPT. A comment only: the object
code is the same.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 166102a..84cb838 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -3066,10 +3066,10 @@ unsigned int dvbridge_render_step_levels(const struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool
      * (whatever level it is drawn at, so that its ladder stays one) */
     if (r && r->scaled_source)
         return residual ? 0xfu : 0xbu;
-    /* Hades: the IPT tunnel, whose level 3 sends the composer's YCbCr instead (no conversion of
-     * its pixels): the last of the levels, the largest change where a display interpolates the
-     * chroma between the pairs (measured: up to 9 to 120 codes of I on pictures of a profile 7
-     * stream with linear interpolation, against at most 15 at level 2) */
+    /* Hades: the IPT tunnel (an expert choice), whose level 3 sends the composer's YCbCr instead
+     * (no conversion of its pixels): the last of the levels, and no loss of fidelity. Measured in
+     * delta E ITP over I, P and T of every pixel of profile 7 pictures, the composer's YCbCr is as
+     * close to the picture as IPT or closer, however a display fills in a pair's right pixel */
     const bool ipt = r && r->source && r->ipt_wanted && dvbridge_source_can_ipt(r->source_packer) &&
                      r->source_params.affine;
     if (residual)
